# Material Guide (v22+)

Target `@angular/material` / `@angular/cdk` versions in `frontend/package.json` (currently ^22). Follow Material 3 token APIs. Private `.mat-mdc-*` selectors are limited to `_material-overrides.scss` and `_components.scss` as described in `docs/STYLING_GUIDELINES.md`. Feature and component stylesheets do not style Material's private DOM.

## Theming source of truth

Project theme lives under `src/styles/`:

| File | Role |
| --- | --- |
| `_theme-colors.scss` | Private Sass color map (`@use` from `_tokens` / `theme` only) |
| `_tokens.scss` | Semantic **color** and **typography** CSS variables |
| `theme.scss` | `mat.theme` + system overrides |
| `_material-overrides.scss` | Global Material look: `mat.*-overrides`, plus `.mat-mdc-*` when the mixin cannot express the style |
| `_components.scss` | App primitives and component-scoped `.mat-mdc-*` |
| `_base.scss`, `_fonts.scss` | Document defaults and font imports |
| `tailwind.css` | Real Tailwind v4; `@theme` bridges colors + fonts; default spacing/radius/shadow scales |

When changing look-and-feel, prefer tokens and these files over one-off component hacks.

## Official theming APIs (required)

```scss
@use '@angular/material' as mat;

html {
  color-scheme: dark; // match app (this project is dark)
  @include mat.theme((
    color: (primary: mat.$cyan-palette, theme-type: dark),
    typography: (...),
    density: 0,
  ));
  @include mat.theme-overrides(( primary: ..., on-primary: ... ));
  @include mat.button-overrides(( filled-container-color: ... ));
}
```

- Define the global theme with **`mat.theme`**.
- Adjust system tokens with **`mat.theme-overrides`** (or `$overrides` on `mat.theme`).
- Adjust a single component with its **`mat.<component>-overrides`** mixin (validated keys at build time).
- In custom UI, consume **`var(--mat-sys-*)`** (and app tokens from `_tokens.scss`) so light/dark and theme updates stay coherent.

## Do / Don't

**Do**

- Use Material components and CDK primitives (`Dialog`, `Overlay`, a11y, table, form-field) instead of reinventing behavior.
- Prefer outlined/filled variants and density already configured in `_material-overrides.scss` (compact trading density `-1`).
- Keep dialogs as focused Material dialogs; reuse existing shared dialogs when possible.
- Preserve accessibility: labels, `aria-*`, focus management, contrast against dark/light trading themes.
- Align custom surfaces with Material system roles and app tokens (`--color-surface`, `--color-primary`, etc.).
- Follow `docs/STYLING_GUIDELINES.md` for density, panels, tables, and buy/sell semantic actions.

**Don't**

- Do not put `.mat-mdc-*`, `::ng-deep`, or `!important` in `*.component.scss` or feature stylesheets. Do not set private `--mat-*` component variables outside the overrides APIs.
- Feature and component stylesheets must not depend on Material internal DOM or class names. `_material-overrides.scss` and `_components.scss` may use `.mat-mdc-*` only as `docs/STYLING_GUIDELINES.md` describes.
- Introduce a second UI kit or ad-hoc button/input system alongside Material.
- Add purple-on-white / generic “AI default” palettes; keep the trading blue + semantic green/red system from `docs/STYLING_GUIDELINES.md`.

## Components & patterns in this app

- Prefer existing shared building blocks under `src/app/shared/components/` before new Material composites.
- Forms: `mat-form-field` + reactive forms; match existing appearance (outline/fill) from nearby screens.
- Feedback: use `NotificationService` (`app-snackbar` stack) instead of inventing another toast path.
- Tables: prefer the shared `data-table` patterns and Material table/sort/paginator conventions already in use.
- Icons: use Material icons consistently with existing navigation and actions.

## Change discipline

- Theme token changes belong in `src/styles`, not scattered component SCSS, unless the style is truly local layout.
- Component SCSS should handle layout/spacing composition; color/shape should come from tokens / Material overrides when shared.
- After Material or theme edits, sanity-check key surfaces: login, dashboard, dialogs, sidebar/navbar, form fields, buttons.
